      <Description>CHECKPOINT BEFORE NGINX

MariaDB:
- Container running
- Database wordpress created
- User wpuser working
- Root password configured via Docker secret
- Persistent named volume: srcs_mariadb_data
- Host data: /home/mgrandia/data/mariadb

WordPress:
- Container running
- PHP-FPM 8.2 working on TCP port 9000
- WordPress files working
- wp-config.php generated
- Persistent named volume: srcs_wordpress_data
- Host data: /home/mgrandia/data/wordpress
- WordPress files owned by www-data

Connectivity:
- WordPress -&gt; MariaDB tested successfully
- PHP mysqli connection returned OK

Docker:
- One inception network
- MariaDB and WordPress have restart: unless-stopped
- Restart of WordPress tested successfully
- No ports exposed yet
- NGINX not configured yet

IMPORTANT:
This snapshot is the known-good state before starting NGINX/TLS.</Description>
